            ("Combined normal-anion-gap metabolic acidosis and respiratory alkalosis", "The respiratory component fits, but the anion gap is elevated. Bicarbonate loss alone, such as diarrhea or renal tubular acidosis, would not produce this electrolyte pattern."),
